    image: "/poi-images/inyati-cities-v2.webp",
    description: {
      "de": "Inyati ist eine historisch bedeutende Missionsstation und Siedlung in Matabeleland North.",
      "hu": "Zimbabwe egyik legrégebbi európai települése, amely eredetileg missziós állomásként jött létre.",
      "ro": "Inyati este o așezare cu o mare importanță istorică, fiind locul primei misiuni creștine din regiune.",
      "en": "Inyati is one of the oldest modern settlements in Zimbabwe, founded in 1859 as a mission station. Located north of Bulawayo, it holds deep historical significance as a cradle of education and early cross-cultural interaction in the region."
    },
    facts: {
      "de": ["Älteste Missionsstation", "Historisch bedeutsam", "In Matabeleland North", "Ländliches Zentrum"],
      "hu": ["1859-ben alapította a Londoni Missziós Társaság", "A zimbabwei kereszténység egyik bölcsője", "Matabeleland North tartományban fekszik", "Történelmi jelentőségű iskola működik itt"],
      "ro": ["Misiune fondată în 1859", "Leagănul creștinismului local", "Centru educațional istoric", "Situat în Matabeleland North"],
      "en": ["Site of Zimbabwe's first mission", "Founded in 1895 by the LMS", "Located in Matabeleland North", "Deeply historic educational center", "Farming and small-scale mining hub", "Located near the town of Turk Mine"]
    },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Inyati ist ein historisch bedeutsamer Ort in der Provinz Matabeleland North in Simbabwe und gilt als Wiege der modernen Bildung und des Christentums im Land. Gegründet wurde die Station im Jahr 1859 von Robert Moffat von der London Missionary Society auf Land, das ihm der Matabele-König Mzilikazi zur Verfügung gestellt hatte. Dies war die erste permanente christliche Mission im heutigen Simbabwe. Die Inyati High School, die aus der ursprünglichen Missionsstation hervorging, ist eine der ältesten Schulen des Landes und hat viele bedeutende Persönlichkeiten hervorgebracht. Neben seiner religiösen und bildungspolitischen Geschichte ist Inyati ein regionales Zentrum für die Landwirtschaft und den kleingewerblichen Bergbau, insbesondere in der Nähe der Turk Mine. Ein Besuch in Inyati bietet tiefe Einblicke in die frühe Kolonialgeschichte und die komplexen Beziehungen zwischen den europäischen Missionaren und dem Matabele-Königreich im 19. Jahrhundert.",
      hu: "Inyati Zimbabwe egyik legfontosabb történelmi helyszíne, amely Matabeleland North tartományban fekszik. A település 1859-ben jött létre, amikor Robert Moffat, a Londoni Missziós Társaság képviselője engedélyt kapott Mzilikazi matabele királytól egy állandó misszió megalapítására. Ez volt az első ilyen jellegű európai intézmény az ország területén, így Inyatit gyakran nevezik a zimbabwei kereszténység és a modern oktatás bölcsőjének. Az itt alapított iskola ma is működik Inyati High School néven, és az ország egyik legtekintélyesebb oktatási intézményeként tartják számon. A település történelmi épületei és a misszió emlékei fontos mementói a 19. századi afrikai missziós tevékenységnek és a helyi törzsi uralkodókkal való kapcsolatoknak. Inyati gazdaságilag ma elsősorban a mezőgazdaságból és a környékbeli bányászatból (például a Turk Mine) él, de szellemi öröksége messze túlmutat a régió határain.",
      ro: "Inyati este o localitate de o importanță istorică crucială în Zimbabwe, situată în provincia Matabeleland North. Fondată în 1859 de către Robert Moffat de la Societatea Misionară din Londra, Inyati reprezintă locul primei misiuni creștine permanente din țară, stabilită cu permisiunea regelui Mzilikazi al poporului Matabele. Acest eveniment a marcat începutul educației formale și a răspândirii creștinismului în regiune, Inyati devenind rapid un centru vital de învățare. Școala fondată aici, Inyati High School, rămâne una dintre cele mai vechi și respectate instituții de învățământ din Zimbabwe, formând generații de lideri. Dincolo de valoarea sa spirituală și istorică, așezarea servește ca centru rural pentru activități agricole și mici exploatări miniere, fiind situată în apropierea minei Turk Mine. O vizită la Inyati oferă o perspectivă fascinantă asupra interacțiunilor timpurii dintre misionarii europeni și regatele africane, păstrând vie moștenirea unei epoci de transformări profunde.",
      en: "Inyati holds a distinguished place in Zimbabwe's history as the site of the country's first permanent Christian mission. Established in 1859 by Robert Moffat of the London Missionary Society, it was built on land granted by King Mzilikazi of the Matabele people. This partnership marked a turning point in the region's history, as Inyati became the cradle of modern education and literacy in Zimbabwe. The mission station eventually evolved into the Inyati High School, which continues to be one of the nation's most prestigious educational institutions today. Located north of Bulawayo in Matabeleland North province, the settlement remains deeply connected to its historic roots, with several colonial-era buildings still standing as witnesses to its past. Economically, Inyati functions as a hub for local farming and small-scale mining enterprises, particularly near the Turk Mine. Its historical significance and enduring educational legacy make it a landmark of cultural development and a key site for understanding Zimbabwe's 19th-century history.",
    },
